Z||000000||Alex4mula||08-08-2000||11:02 AM||||I'm looking to upgrade my Formula sound system. I'm planning to put 5 1/4 in front, tweeters in pillars, 4x6 and a sub. <BR> Do 5 1/4 really fit in front without major hassle?<BR>I would like to put Infinity speakers but I'm not sure if selecting the Reference series or the Kappa. The difference in price for all except the sub would be $190.<BR> Do anyone knows from experience (hearing them) if the Kappa sounds very noticeably better than the Reference? <BR>The sub will be an Infinity Perfect 10 mounted in the footwell. Would 200W would be enough amp power for this sub? There is a 5 channel amp (4 x 50 + 200 x1) that I would like but not sure if the sub power will be enough. The sub is very efficient (94db). Your opinions are welcome. Thanks  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||b lo 0||08-08-2000||11:16 AM||||As far as I know, the Kappas have way less distortion and crisper highs.  I'm getting the References though because I'm on a budget<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT (in progress)  <BR>titled ICE-plates B LO 0 <BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.angelfire.com/ga3/audioimagery/ice.gif">     <BR>Go to <A HREF="http://www.audioimagery.i-p.com" TARGET=_blank>www.audioimagery.i-p.com</A>  !!!<P><A HREF="http://clubs.excite.com/welcome/main?cid=.zXb1DJ1lsCL&aid=22&auth=" TARGET=_blank>Pontiac Fiero Owner's Club</A>-Pics, Videos and More-Or Post your Own||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||08-08-2000||11:30 AM||||I bought the Infinity Kappa 4 X 6 plates for the sail panels. (has a 3 1/2 woofer and seperate tweeter) I think the plate speakers for the 4 X 6 sound better than the oval shaped speakers. As for the front I'm going with Polk Audio EX series. I think they sound better than the Infinity Kappa's. I'm going with the 4". When you get your 5 1/4's installed take some pics, I'd like to see how they turn out. The Infinity Kappa's sound much better than the reference series.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fiero56||08-08-2000||01:14 PM||||I have been trying to decide what to do with the current stock setup in my Formula. I bought the Infinity Kappa 4x6 plate for the rear, and a nice pair of 6x9 Boston Acoustics for the dash. Hopefully these suckers pump out enough bass for my taste, eliminating the need for a sub. If I still want more bass, I will add a sub, to the rest of the system I have waiting to go in; Pioneer single din headunit(DEHP-5200), and Clarion ProAudio 5 channel amp. I will be adding a changer later.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Alex4mula||08-08-2000||02:05 PM||||Cool... So the Kappas are a lot better... I'll try to go with them then. <BR>I remember someone here instaled 5 1/4 in front and said only minor mods required. I measured and it seems like they may fit but not sure. There is a 5 channel Infinity amp in Crutchfield that pumps out 50W x 4 and 200W x 1. The 50W I know are Ok fro front and back but not sure about the 200W for the Perfect 10.||||reg||11
Z||000005||Standard||08-09-2000||12:53 AM||||I just put in a DEH-P5200 about 2 months ago, and I love it!  I also have Pioneer 2-way 4x10's and 4x6's replacing the stock speakers, and a 10" pioneer sub waiting to go in as soon as I figure out what kinda box I wanna use.  <P>I'm thinking about going to 5 1/4's in the front and a 4x6 plate in the rear, as soon as I get some money saved up.  <P>------------------<BR>Mike -- Golden Valley, MN<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 148,000 miles and counting!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Philphine||08-09-2000||03:28 AM||||i have 5 1/4' components in pods in the dead pedal area. i use the 4x10 spot to hold the x overs for it.<P>i have infinity kappa and reference subs but have not made use of the references yet. the kappas are in my blazer and sound very good.<P>also have some 8" reference 3 ways that i mean to try to get into my next fiero. ||||reg||1
